 "description": "T21 TiDB 8.5 sequence lifecycle and restart oracles. The manifest pins the frozen A1 contract: typed sequence options are definition parameters, never runtime issuance progress; SQL RESTART / RESTART WITH carries a bounded warning plus a runtime-issuance evidence gap; CYCLE enablement warns on declared or catalog-proven state; drop warns only on a vouched inbound-reference set; sequence identity shares the table namespace; multi-target DROP adjudicates per member without all-or-nothing rollback; reader errors propagate uncached; unvouched identity yields unknown_sequence_state, never a fabricated absent. metadata_cases encode the native probes whose oracles still require the isolated TiDB 8.5 environment — none of them has run and none may be claimed as native PASS. CLI cases are provider-free offline contracts. Runtime allocator, cache consumption, current/next value, and persisted progress are deferred to A2 and appear nowhere in this manifest.",
